{"duration_api_ms":320890,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"5665fe0a-cbcd-42bc-99f1-af7274b9f860","total_cost_usd":0.36138400000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14550,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":30318,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":24743},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14550,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":30318,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14550},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":30318,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":14550,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.36138400000000004,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":24743,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"Both objectives are dominated by one corner of the design space. Every feasible front point has cone angle 70 (the upper bound), bluntness 1.15-1.2 and D 3.25-3.36 m. Temperature is what moves hypervolume: the flux reference is 2.5e6 W/m2, so flux differences of about 40k barely matter, while 1 K of bondline temperature is worth about 0.006 normalised HV. From the margins, the limits are max_g <= 12.0 and heatshield mass fraction, which behaves like margin ~ 0.0497 + 0.028*(b-1.2) - 0.5855*(D-3.3). This puts the D ceiling near 3.385 m and makes the mass margin almost independent of gamma and cone. Peak g is set mainly by gamma (about 1.8 g/deg near -3.55) with a small positive D dependence (about 0.53 g/m). Larger D lowers both flux and temperature (about -16 K/m in T, flux roughly D^-1.3), and steeper gamma lowers T at about 1 K per 0.1 deg. The best corner is therefore D about 3.375-3.383, b about 1.2, cone 70, gamma about -3.55 to -3.565. Geometry failures occur for b >= 1.3 and for lower cone angles at high b. Bluntness 1.22 fails the cd_fore hull at cone 70, so b must stay at or below about 1.2-1.21.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-cbb67c388863 (D3.3,b1.2,g-3.55): T392.78, g11.933, mass margin 0.0497. C-6b7d0d55c053 (D3.34,b1.15): mass margin 0.02513. C-0e7e9141529e (D3.36,b1.15): 0.01342. These fit the linear-in-D mass-margin law, so D <= 3.384 at b1.2.\",\"C-9dee12ef8e1a (D3.28,g-3.55) 11.923, C-a07aa6172ab6 (D3.3,g-3.53) 11.898, C-59753de6b401 (D3.25,g-3.58) 11.961, C-a7cedecd1f0d (D3.22,g-3.6) 11.981 give dg/dgamma about -1.8 per deg and dg/dD about +0.5 per m, so the g limit at D3.38 is about gamma -3.56.\",\"C-a07aa6172ab6 (D3.3,b1.18) T393.11 vs C-9dee12ef8e1a (D3.28,b1.18) T393.27 vs C-cbb67c388863 (D3.3,b1.2) T392.78 show that larger D and b lower T and that b is a weak lever.\",\"C-1b507004c89c and C-de929f2046c9 (b1.22, cone70) fail the cd_fore hull; C-9c1cc1a27672, C-ec5b30508673, C-ca010b12fec4 (b1.35) and C-f986776067bd (b1.3, cone 69) are invalid geometries. b is capped near 1.2 at cone 70.\",\"Shallow-gamma points C-e735d4570166 (241k, 421 K), C-30939dece9a3 and C-d916d7265dfe (252k, 409 K) and the steep corner C-cbb67c388863 (284k, 392.8 K) leave gaps in the staircase between gamma -2.2 and -3.3, and none of them uses D above 3.36.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation flux falls with nose radius and with lower ballistic coefficient (larger D), so D at its mass-fraction ceiling and the largest valid b minimise flux. Bondline temperature tracks heat load, which falls with a shorter and steeper pulse, so gamma should sit just inside the g limit. Because g rises only slightly with D while T falls with D, pushing D to about 3.38 and backing gamma off by about 0.02 deg gives a net T drop of about 1 K. Re-running the whole gamma sweep at D3.375 dominates the older D3.2-3.3 front points and fills the staircase gaps.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The mass margin at D 3.38-3.383 is only 0.001-0.003 and the linear fit could be off by that much, so those designs may violate heatshield_mass_fraction. The g margin at gamma -3.56/-3.568 is under 0.1%, and the local slope in gamma is only roughly known. b of 1.205-1.21 may hit the cd_fore hull failure. Flux and T predictions come from eyeballed local fits (D^-1.3 for flux, about -16 K/m and about 1 K per 0.1 deg for T). They are less certain at shallow gamma, where the T slope is steeper (about 1.3-1.6 K per 0.1 deg).\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Corner candidate: D near the mass ceiling and gamma just inside the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Most likely to improve the T end of the front by about 1.4 K; tests both the mass and g margins near their limits.\",\"requested_fidelity\":1},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Slightly smaller D for a bigger mass margin, with the same steep gamma.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Safer version of the corner candidate; secures a feasible improvement.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Test the mass-fraction boundary at D 3.383 while keeping gamma at -3.55 for g margin.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.383,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the D ceiling precisely; a feasible result gives the lowest T of this batch.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.36 with a slightly steeper gamma to trade the g margin for T.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.565},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":278200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.65,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Probes the g-limit boundary with a comfortable mass margin.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.38 with b 1.19 to separate the b effect from the D effect on T and flux.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.19,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.55,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks how much b matters at high D and provides a fallback if b 1.2 is too close to a limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Probe the b upper limit (cd_fore hull) at 1.21.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.21,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"b 1.22 failed the hull check while 1.2 passed; this maps the edge and may yield about 0.1 K of extra T reduction.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate b of 1.205 at D 3.38.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.205,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"A less risky probe of the hull boundary, only 0.005 above the known-good b of 1.2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"D 3.35 with gamma -3.568 to sample the g-limit boundary at a lower D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.35,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.568},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":279300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Gives another point on the D-gamma trade-off near the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e735d4570166\",\"rationale\":\"Shallowest gamma at larger D to extend the low-flux end of the front.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229600,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":419.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Larger D lowers flux by about 5% compared with C-e735d4570166 and extends the front leftwards.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill at D 3.375, gamma -1.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":415.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the shallow-gamma section and dominates C-30939dece9a3 and C-95fec46a4ac3.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill at D 3.375, gamma -2.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":240500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Dominates the D3.25-3.3 points at gamma -1.9 and -2.2.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill at D 3.375, gamma -2.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.25},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":246000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Improves on C-d916d7265dfe, which has 252k W/m2 and 409 K.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill in the empty gamma range between -2.2 and -3.3.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":251700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"The staircase currently jumps from 252k/409 K to 273k/394.5 K, so intermediate points add area.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill at gamma -2.65.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":255300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the mid-front gap and checks whether flux and T are smooth in gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill at gamma -2.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":258800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Mid-front point that should dominate C-3557b5bcc316 and C-aee66ec2a89b.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill at gamma -2.95.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.95},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extra coverage of the mid-front in the region where the front currently has no points.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill at gamma -3.1.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":266000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Dominates C-5d7a821d8a55 (276.6k, 396.5 K) via larger D.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Front fill at gamma -3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":268500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the gap between the mid-front and the steep corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Should dominate C-0e7e9141529e (273k, 394.55 K) with larger D and b1.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Low-risk improvement of an existing front point.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cbb67c388863\",\"rationale\":\"Robust feasible point with a comfortable g margin (gamma -3.45) at high D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Low-risk near-corner point that hedges against the tight g margin of the more aggressive candidates.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":274416,"type":"result","duration_ms":321066,"uuid":"932a595a-8806-45ba-9cf9-5da5c2b823e3","ttft_stream_ms":1398,"time_to_request_ms":174,"first_content_frame_ms":1398,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
